{
  "about": [
    "The font page's glossary (site/index.html, 6. Glossary): its sections and each one's rows, in page order.",
    "The Builder edits the rows in Glyphs > Glossary; `cd builder && python3 -m jzpbuild.glossary` then rewrites the",
    "tables between the <!-- glossary <id> --> markers (a release does it too); headings and text around them stay as written.",
    "A section's key is its id, and its title starts with it (\"1c: Left Hand Techniques\").",
    "A row is a glyph, {\"glyph\": \"lg_gou\"}, or a word written together, {\"word\": \"少息\", \"glyphs\": [\"md_shao\", \"md_xi\"]};",
    "its ASCII, 中文 and 拼音 come from the glyphs' spellings in builder/inputs/components.csv. \"meaning\" (optional) fills",
    "the Meaning column, which a section gets once one of its rows has a meaning. \"typed\" (optional) is what was typed to add or edit the row.",
    "Every glyph with spellings is in some section, on its own or in a word; 99: Hidden in Glossary leaves one out on purpose.",
    "kind 'usage': ASCII | 中文 | 拼音 | an example word. `usage` is the section's example as [ASCII, 中文]; {} is the glyph's",
    "spelling, marked red; <r>…</r> marks more. A row's own \"usage\" (the Builder's Example column) replaces it. Words don't go here.",
    "kind 'vertical': each spelling after a colon, typed on its own (a row's own \"usage\" is shown instead). Consecutive numbers (md_1 to md_13) share one row.",
    "kind 'hidden': no table and no marker on the page."
  ],
